ok - a live paused worker stays absorbed until its declared time, then rechecks
ok - a declared wait is not wedge-escalated by a working verdict, while an elapsed declaration and an undeclared lane both keep the unchanged ladder
ok - a default-key answer leaves a keyless wait standing, while the worker's own keyless resolved line retracts it
ok - a declared-wait deferral resets wedge backoff so the lane re-escalates at the base threshold once the wait ends
ok - a captain-held lane is rechecked as a hold on the captain, never as an external wait, and never at all while the captain is away
ok - a backlog captain hold bounds the wedge ladder like a captain-held line, and stays silent while the captain is away
ok - a gate awaiting firstmate's decision for its own run is rechecked on the long cadence in either posture, while a crewmate-owed gate, an unrelated open decision and a runless verdict keep the unchanged ladder
ok - a parked human-owed gate is deferred only while its decision is still open, so an answered-but-unrelayed gate, an unescalated one, and one holding only a blocker all keep the unchanged ladder
ok - with config/wedge-defer-parked-gate absent a parked gate keeps the unchanged ladder, wording and reads
ok - in an armed home a worker's own open newest blocker or decision is deferred to the bounded recheck, and a newer line, a resolved line, a reserved key, or a newer acknowledged inbox record keeps the ladder
ok - with config/wedge-defer-worker-wait absent a worker blocker keeps the byte-identical wedge reason
ok - a wait record missing a field the recheck must print, or carrying one it must not, is refused and the lane escalates exactly as it would have
ok - a running or fixing validation run is deferred on the long recheck cadence rather than wedge-escalated
